    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "LONDON\nDONG KINGMAN",
      "Cocktailo\nSherry Dubonnet Campari\nManhattan Gin Martini Vodka Martini Vermouth\nBloody Mary Screwdriver Whiskey Sour\nTom Collins Vodka Collins Daiquiri Scotch Bourbon\nCanadian Gin Vodka Rum\nPremium Beer\nMenus\nApéritif\nHors d'Oeuvre Gastronomiques\nSelected gourmet delicacies\nFilet Mignon Grillé, Beurre Raifort\nBroiled tenderloin with horseradish butter\nRagoût d'Agneau à l'Indienne\nLamb Curry\nSuprême de Volaille Normande\nBoneless breast of chicken stuffed with apples and almonds\nHomard Thermidor\nLobster Thermidor\nPommes de Terre Maison\nPotatoes Maison\nLégumes au Beurre\nButtered vegetable bouquet\nSalade Campagnarde",
      "Boneless breast of chicken stuffed with apples and almonds\nHomard Thermidor\nLobster Thermidor\nPommes de Terre Maison\nPotatoes Maison\nLégumes au Beurre\nButtered vegetable bouquet\nSalade Campagnarde\nTossed garden salad\nSélection de Fruits et Fromages\nSelected fruits and cheeses\nDessert\nCafé\nCoffee\nCafé Décaféiné\nDecaffeinated Coffee\nThé\nTea\nSelected Red and White Wines\nChampagne Brut\nDrambuieT Amaretto di Saronno\nCrème de Menthe Cognac VSOP\nCointreau\nBénédictine\n105.K433",
      "Dong Kingman, the award winning Chinese-American artist, travels the world sketching and painting\nthe beautiful, the monumental and the picturesque. His watercolors grace more than forty\npermanent museum and private collections in the USA and abroad.\nThis view of the Thames embankment and Big Ben captures some of the charm of London. Every\nstudent of history should see the Houses of Parliament, Buckingham Palace, Westminster Abbey, and\nthe Tower of London. While it is one of the world's great centers of commerce, it is also a city of\nbeauty with extensive parks and gardens. The luxurious Inter-Continental London is situated adjacent\nto gracious Hyde Park and the Portman Inter-Continental Hotel is conveniently located at One,\nPortman Square. Pan Am serves London every day on its Round-The-World flights and one can reach\nLondon on Pan Am from virtually anywhere in the world\nANAM.\n2010.011. 008"
    ],
